Wallet of perseus is quite nice to have, but not required. a really
good aritwish early on too..make sure to get it blessed

=oSD is a must for vampires...

medicine bag is not a bad idea at all, although i don't think BUC
affects it for drawing blood (nto sure though,and you canwish for it
blessed anyway).  at your current level + medicine bag you may be able
to protection racket quite easily.

About your whisperfeet...you want magic resistance befroe you wish for
them, and even then hold on until you have more hp.  If i remember
correctly, with MR, non intelligent artifacts still blast you for like
4d6 (or maybe 6d6, probably 6d6), which is a lot at your current level,
although you have regen to coutner that.  also, considering the only
bonus you get here is stealth, it's not that much better than regular
speed boots, and saves you and artiwish for later. if you're gonna wish
for an artifact, make it big. (unless i'm missing something really
awesome about stealth...)

IIRC (spoiler check confrimed this), Necromancers don't get ANY skill
in divination, and with identify being a level FIVE spell in nethack,
it's quite a poor wish early on in the game (or really, later on).

HoB...oddly enough i would hold off on.  you may find one in the mall,
or in the mines, or even dwarf helm + GL it.  with 18 intelligence, you
really won't be needing it for a while, i don't think.

SDSM is a good idea, regardless, as is a [oMR.

gauntlets of dexterity (alternatively gauntlets of defence, if you can
handle the blast, although, like the whisper feet, the halfed physical
damage is taken care of later by hand of vecna, so choose wisely.)

charging: naturally.

as far as distance attacking goes, you're gonna be expert in attack
spells, so you'll be fine.

if you really want (i do this, although i doubt you'll see ANYONE else
suggest it, it's not realyl too smart of an idea, i just like it), wish
up a sniper rifle, then later get crowned with it.  you only have like
a 40% chance of it appearing in the game.
but again, a bunch of silver daggers is probably a much better idea.

?oIdentify: i highly suggest against these. a magic marker is a better
idea, sounds like you ID'ed identify scrolls already, and even if you
haven't, you will really soon, so it's not THAT long a wait to id
stuff.

make damn sure the wand isn't cursed first though :D

